\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All thanks be to God,
\par Who scatters abroad,
\par Throughout every place,
\par By the least of His servants, 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par His saviour of grace.
\par Who the victory gave,
\par The praise let Him have,
\par \pard\tx3780 For the work He hath  done :
\par All honour and glory to Jesus alone !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our conquering Lord 
\par Hath prospered His word,
\par Hath made it prevail, 
\par And mightily shaken the kingdom of hell
\par His arm He hath bared,
\par And a people prepared 
\par His glory to show,
\par And witness the power of His passion below.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He hath opened a door 
\par To the penitent poor,
\par And rescued from sin,
\par And admitted the harlots and publicans in ;
\par They have heard the glad sound, 
\par They have liberty found
\par Through the blood of the Lamb,
\par And plentiful pardon in Jesus's name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And shall we not sing
\par Our Saviour and King ? 
\par Thy witnesses, we
\par With rapture ascribe our salvation to Thee.
\par Thou, Jesus, hast blessed,
\par And believers increased,
\par Who thankfully own
\par We are freely forgiven through mercy alone
\par 
\par \pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. His Spirit revives
\par His work in our lives,
\par His wonders of grace,
\par So mightily wrought in the primitive days.
\par O that all men might know
\par His tokens below,
\par Our Saviour confess,
\par And embrace the glad tidings of pardon and peace !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thou Saviour of all,
\par Effectually call
\par The sinners that stray ;
\par And O let a nation be born in a day ! 
\par Then , then let it spread 
\par Thy knowledge  and dread,
\par And the universe filled with  the glory of God.\tab 
\par                                                   Amen.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

